  "Specification": "This specification models a simple system where a variable x is an array indexed by a domain Dom, which is a union of two integer ranges. The system repeatedly increments x[i] modulo K for some i in Dom, and in each step, it awaits the existence of a subset s of 1..L with cardinality L. The variable y is also present and can take values in 1..C, allowing for multiple initial states. The comments explain the state space size and the computational cost of evaluating the next-state action, emphasizing the exponential blowup due to the power set operation. The spec is designed to stress-test model checking tools like TLC, especially with respect to set and function operations.",
